---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | MyGreekTax"
  description="How MyGreekTax collects, uses, and protects your personal data."
  canonicalPath="/privacy/"
>
  <main style="max-width:720px;margin:0 auto;padding:4rem 1.5rem;font-family:'DM Sans',sans-serif;color:#28251d;">
    <a href="/" style="font-size:0.875rem;color:#C9923A;text-decoration:none;">← Back to MyGreekTax</a>
    <h1 style="font-family:'Playfair Display',serif;font-size:2.5rem;margin:1.5rem 0 0.5rem;">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p style="color:#7a7974;margin-bottom:2.5rem;">Last updated: 28 July 2026</p>
    <h2 style="font-size:1.25rem;margin:2rem 0 0.5rem;">1. Who We Are</h2>
    <p>MyGreekTax is operated by Dimitrios Gkikas, a licensed Greek tax professional. Contact: <a href="mailto:hello@mygreektax.eu" style="color:#C9923A;">hello@mygreektax.eu</a></p>
    <h2 style="font-size:1.25rem;margin:2rem 0 0.5rem;">2. Data We Collect</h2>
    <p>When you submit the consultation form we collect your name, email address, and the details you provide. We do not collect payment information on this site.</p>
    <p style="margin-top:0.75rem;">If you go on to become a client, we also hold the case information you send us — correspondence, documents, and the details needed for the filings you have asked us to handle — in our client portal at portal.mygreektax.eu. If you choose to use our secure credential form, we additionally hold an encrypted copy of the TAXISnet details you submit through it. Section 4 explains that in full.</p>
    <h2 style="font-size:1.25rem;margin:2rem 0 0.5rem;">3. How We Use Your Data</h2>
    <p>Your data is used solely to respond to your enquiry and to carry out the work you have engaged us for. We do not sell, rent, or share your personal data with third parties except where required by law or where necessary to deliver the service you asked for — principally our licensed Greek accountant partner, who carries out regulated filings under a formal authorisation you grant.</p>
    <h2 id="taxisnet-credentials" style="font-size:1.25rem;margin:2rem 0 0.5rem;scroll-margin-top:100px;">4. TAXISnet Credentials (Optional)</h2>
    <p>We do not need your TAXISnet password in order to act for you. The standard route is a formal <em>εξουσιοδότηση</em> (authorisation) that you grant through myAADE, scoped to the specific filing. Your account stays under your sole control, and this remains our recommended approach.</p>
    <p style="margin-top:0.75rem;">Some clients would rather we register that authorisation on their behalf than do it themselves. Where you ask us to, we send you a one-time link to a secure form on our portal. Using it is entirely voluntary and is never a condition of any service. If you do use it, this is exactly what happens:</p>
    <ul style="padding-left:1.5rem;line-height:1.9;margin-top:0.75rem;">
      <li><strong>What we ask for.</strong> Your AFM, AMKA, TAXISnet username and password, any two-factor detail needed to complete the login, and any note you want to add.</li>
      <li><strong>It is encrypted in your browser.</strong> The form encrypts your submission on your own device, before anything is transmitted (RSA-OAEP-4096 with AES-256-GCM). What our database receives, and all it is ever able to hold, is unreadable ciphertext.</li>
      <li><strong>Our systems cannot read it.</strong> The key that decrypts your submission is held outside them entirely: not in our database, not in our hosting provider's configuration, not in our source code, and not in any environment variable. It is entered by hand into a single administrator's browser at the moment a submission is opened, and is discarded when that page is reloaded.</li>
      <li><strong>It is used for one purpose.</strong> To register the authorisation for the service you asked about, and for nothing else.</li>
      <li><strong>It is not shared.</strong> Not with our accountant partner, who works through the authorisation rather than through your password, and not with anyone else.</li>
      <li><strong>Every access is recorded.</strong> Each time a submission is opened or deleted, we log who did it, when, and which service justified it.</li>
      <li><strong>Time limits apply.</strong> The link expires 30 days after we issue it and can be revoked sooner. A submission is deleted 180 days after it is made, or earlier at your request. Submitting again replaces and erases the previous submission.</li>
      <li><strong>You can withdraw at any time.</strong> Our lawful basis for holding these details is your explicit consent (GDPR Article 6(1)(a)). Email <a href="mailto:hello@mygreektax.eu" style="color:#C9923A;">hello@mygreektax.eu</a> and we will delete the submission and confirm that we have done so.</li>
    </ul>
    <p style="margin-top:0.75rem;">If you have shared your password with us, we recommend changing it once the authorisation is in place. We will never ask for your TAXISnet password by email, by phone, or through any messaging app, and you should not send it that way. The only channel we use is the encrypted form described above.</p>
    <h2 style="font-size:1.25rem;margin:2rem 0 0.5rem;">5. Third-Party Services</h2>
    <ul style="padding-left:1.5rem;line-height:2;">
      <li><strong>Make (Celonis Labs BV)</strong> — receives and routes consultation form submissions to our internal client system. See <a href="https://www.make.com/en/privacy-notice" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:#C9923A;">their privacy policy</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>Supabase</strong> — the database behind our client portal, where client and case records are stored. Encrypted credential submissions are stored here as ciphertext only.</li>
      <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> — hosts and serves this site and our client portal.</li>
      <li><strong>Mailgun (Sinch)</strong> — delivers the email we send you about your case.</li>
      <li><strong>Plausible Analytics</strong> — cookie-free, GDPR-compliant analytics. No personal data stored.</li>
      <li><strong>Google Fonts</strong> — fonts loaded from Google's CDN; your IP may be logged by Google.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2 style="font-size:1.25rem;margin:2rem 0 0.5rem;">6. Cookies</h2>
    <p>This site does not use tracking cookies. Plausible Analytics operates without cookies. See our <a href="/cookies/" style="color:#C9923A;">Cookie Policy</a>.</p>
    <h2 style="font-size:1.25rem;margin:2rem 0 0.5rem;">7. Your Rights (GDPR)</h2>
    <p>You have the right to access, rectify, or erase any personal data we hold about you, and to withdraw any consent you have given. Email <a href="mailto:hello@mygreektax.eu" style="color:#C9923A;">hello@mygreektax.eu</a>.</p>
    <h2 style="font-size:1.25rem;margin:2rem 0 0.5rem;">8. Data Retention</h2>
    <p>Enquiry data is retained for up to 3 years unless you request earlier deletion. Encrypted TAXISnet credential submissions are retained for 180 days and then deleted, or sooner on request, as described in section 4.</p>
    <h2 style="font-size:1.25rem;margin:2rem 0 0.5rem;">9. Changes</h2>
    <p>We may update this policy occasionally. The "last updated" date at the top will reflect any changes.</p>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
